        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-23T15:31:26+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-23T15:31:26+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-23T06:01:26Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T06:01:26Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge westwards over central and eastern SA and a low pressure trough extends from WA over western SA. This trough will be very slow-moving for the rest of the week and over the weekend and the ridge will move away to the east. A weakening cold front will slip across southern coasts late Thursday and early Friday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
            </forecast-period>
